 "text": "Recorder's Office General Information - Sac County, Iowa\nSkip to content\n-->\n--> Search\nAbout -->\nBoards & Commissions\nCemeteries\nCommunities\nElected Officials\nSchool Districts\nTownship Information\nDepartments -->\nAmbulance Service\nAssessor\nAuditor\nBoard of Supervisors\nConservation\nCounty Attorney\nE-911\nEmergency Management\nGeneral Assistance\nHuman Resources\nMedical Examiner\nPlanning and Zoning\nPublic Health -->\nRecorder\nRoadside Program\nSecondary Roads\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nVeterans Affairs\nResources -->\nBid Notices\nCalendar\nCareers\nCourts -->\nFAQ\nLandfill\nNews\nNotifications\nContact\nSearch Sac County, Iowa\nType 2 or more characters for results.\n-->\nDepartments\nRecorder\nLocation\nRecorder's Office\n100 NW. State St.\nSac City, IA 50583\nDriving Directions -->\nContact Information\n712-662-7789\nRecorder@saccountyiowa.gov\nHours\nM-F | 8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nHoliday Closures\nOur Team\nLaura McKeever\nRecorder\nBethany Burns\nDeputy\nAmber Lucht\nClerk\nVital Records\n-->\nBirth Records\n-->\nDeath Records\n-->\nMarriage License\n-->\nMarriage Records\nRecording Information\n-->\nDocument Formatting Standards\n-->\nMilitary Records\n-->\nRecorder Forms\n-->\nRecording of Documents\n-->\nTransfer Tax Calculator\nLand Records\n-->\nIowa Land Records\n-->\nProperty Search (Beacon)\nDNR\n-->\nHunting & Fishing Licenses\n-->\nRecreational Vehicles\n-->\nPassports\n-->\nNews\nFrequently Asked Questions\n-->\nFAQ\nThe office of the Sac County Recorder was created in 1839 by the first Legislative Assembly of the Territory of Iowa. The Recorder continues to maintain official records of documents affecting title to real estate. One of the major duties of the office is the management of public records, so accuracy and responsible preservation of records are a must for the Recorder. The instruments that are recorded are not only important for today but also serve as a historical library for all of the tomorrows. The office is a service-oriented office with a large variety of duties.\nThe Sac County Recorder's Office DOES NOT:\nProvide legal services\nPrepare legal documents\nMap & Directions\n&q=100+NW.+State+St.,+Sac+City,+IA+50583&zoom=14\" allowfullscreen=\"\">\nAddress\n100 N W State Street\nSac City, IA 50583\nContact Us\nCourthouse Hours\nM-F 8:00 am to 4:30 pm\nClosed Holidays\nDepartment Hours May Vary\n©2026 Sac County | Title VI\npowered by\nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\nVeteran's Day (November 11, 2026)\nThanksgiving (November 26, 2026)\nThanksgiving (November 27, 2026)\nChristmas Eve (December 24, 2026)\nChristmas (December 25, 2026)\nNew Years Day (January 1, 2027)",
